      "- free, pro bono and legal aid, unless you offer it",
      "- jobs, careers, training contract, salary, course and degree",
      "- template, DIY and form, depending on the practice area",
      "- names of towns and regions you do not cover",
      "- complaints, ombudsman and regulator, where the person is unlikely to be looking to instruct",
      "Treat the list as a living document. Each week, add new irrelevant terms and look for good searches you could target more directly with their own ad group.",
      "## Ads and landing pages that earn the enquiry",
      "Responsive search ads should speak to the problem and the next step: what you handle, where, how quickly someone will respond and how to get started. Use assets for call buttons, locations, sitelinks to key services and callouts such as fixed fees or a free initial call, if you genuinely offer them.",
      "Send each ad group to a page about that specific matter, not your homepage. A good legal landing page:",
      "- Opens with the problem the person searched for and confirms you handle it in their area.",
      "- Explains your process and fees clearly, consistent with the price information you publish under the SRA Transparency Rules.",
      "- Shows who they will speak to, with real names and photos of your team.",
      "- Includes accreditations, reviews and experience you can evidence.",
      "- Offers a short form, a click-to-call number and, where suitable, live chat.",
      "- Loads quickly and works well on a phone, where many legal searches happen.",
      "Make sure every claim complies with the SRA Code of Conduct and the advertising codes. Avoid promising outcomes, and be careful with words like specialist or expert unless you can back them up.",
      "## Track clients, not clicks, and answer fast",
      "The biggest gap in most legal accounts is tracking. Google Ads can see form fills and calls, but not which of those became instructed clients. Without that, smart bidding optimises for enquiries of any quality, including the ones your team spends time declining.",
