      "## What has changed",
      "Pay-per-click advertising used to be a manual craft. Account managers set bids keyword by keyword, wrote ads line by line and adjusted budgets by hand. Today the platforms do much of that work themselves with machine learning. Google Ads and Meta set bids in real time for each auction, assemble ads from the headlines and images you provide and find audiences you never explicitly targeted.",
      "That shifts the job. Running PPC well is now less about pulling levers and more about giving the platforms the right inputs: clear goals, accurate conversion data, strong creative and sensible limits. AI also helps outside the platforms, with research, copywriting, analysis and reporting.",
      "## Where the platforms already use AI",
      "- Smart bidding: strategies such as maximise conversions, target CPA and target ROAS set a bid for every auction based on signals like device, location, time of day and the search itself.",
      "- Broad match: matches your keywords to searches with a similar meaning, relying on conversion data to judge what is relevant.",
      "- Responsive search ads: combine your headlines and descriptions into the version most likely to perform for each search.",
      "- Performance Max and Advantage+ campaigns: run across many placements at once, with the platform choosing where and to whom ads are shown.",
      "- Audience expansion: finds new people who resemble those who have already converted.",
      "These tools can work very well. They also do exactly what you tell them to, and that is the catch.",
      "## Why inputs matter more than ever",
      "Smart bidding optimises for the conversions you report. If you count every form fill equally, it will chase the cheapest form fills, including spam, job seekers and people outside your area. If you report which enquiries became clients, and what they were worth, it will chase those instead.",
      "For service businesses, this is the most important change to make:",
      "- Track every enquiry type separately: calls, forms, chats and bookings.",
      "- Record outcomes in your CRM: qualified, booked, won or lost, and the value.",
      "- Send those outcomes back to the platforms as offline conversions.",
      "- Use enhanced conversions and Consent Mode so measurement stays accurate and compliant with UK privacy rules.",
      "Once the platform learns what a good client looks like, automation starts working for you rather than against you.",
      "## Where AI helps outside the platforms",
      "### Research and planning",
      "AI tools can cluster thousands of search terms by intent, summarise the messages competing ads use and draft a campaign structure for review. A specialist still makes the decisions, but the groundwork takes hours instead of days.",
      "### Ad copy and creative",
      "Language models can draft many headline and description options in your tone of voice, ready for testing. AI video and image tools can produce creative variations for Meta, YouTube and TikTok. Volume of variation matters, because the platforms need options to learn from.",
      "### Analysis and anomaly detection",
      "Scripts and AI analysis can flag unusual changes in cost, conversion rate or search terms before they turn into wasted spend, and summarise performance in plain English for people who do not live in the ad accounts.",
      "### Landing page testing",
      "AI helps produce and test variations of landing page copy and layout, so the click lands somewhere that converts. Paying for good traffic and sending it to a weak page is a common and expensive leak.",
      "## Where humans still matter",
      "- Strategy: which services to promote, at what margins, in which locations, and what a client is actually worth.",
      "- Guardrails: negative keywords, brand safety settings, budget caps and exclusions that stop automation drifting.",
      "- Judgement: reading search terms and placements to spot poor-quality traffic the algorithm treats as fine.",
      "- Creative direction: knowing what your customers care about and what makes you different from the firm down the road.",
      "- Compliance: making sure ads meet platform policies and sector rules, such as SRA requirements for law firms or the advertising codes on health claims.",
      "The best results come from combining machine scale with human judgement, not choosing one over the other.",
      "## Common mistakes, and how to avoid them",
